url":"https://github.com/eslint/eslint/pull/7870.patch","merged_at":"2017-01-10T05:09:06Z"},"body":"**What is the purpose of this pull request? (put an \"X\" next to item)**\r\n\r\n[x] Bug fix (see https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7869)\r\n\r\n**What changes did you make? (Give an overview)**\r\n\r\nThis makes a few changes to `brace-style`:\r\n\r\n* It unifies the logic for all types of braced statements into a single function. Previously, there was a lot of code duplication, which led to inconsistencies like https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7869 and https://github.com/eslint/eslint/issues/7869#issuecomment-270802875.\r\n* It changes the report type to report the curly brace token itself, rather than a node in the general vicinity. For example, the previous version of the rule would report the `IfStatement` node here:\r\n\r\n```js\r\n/* eslint brace-style: error */\r\nif (foo) {\r\n\r\n  // ...lots of code\r\n\r\n  bar(); } // <-- there is an issue with this brace, but the `IfStatement` is the node that gets reported\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Is there anything you'd like reviewers to focus on?**\r\n\r\nNothing in particular\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7870/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/7870/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":916996090,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50OTE2OTk2MDkw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/eslint/eslint/issues/events/916996090","actor":{"login":"not-an-aardvark","id":11638619,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjM4NjE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11638619?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/not-an-aardvark","html_url":"https://github.com/not-an-aardvark","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/not-an-aardvark/followers","following_url":"https://ap